{
  "summary": "FIRE（Financial Independence, Retire Early）运动的核心是通过高强度储蓄和投资实现提前退休和财富自由。其标准定义是：在工作时储蓄大部分收入，以便在较年轻时获得财务自由并享受长期退休生活。原则包括：储蓄率通常达到50%以上，优先利用退休账户和应税账户，以及采用4%规则作为安全提款率。4%规则最初基于30年退休期，但FIRE投资者（退休期可能长达50年以上）需调整该规则，包括使用前瞻性回报预测、设定合适的退休期限、降低费用、分散投资以及采用动态支出策略。",
  "key_excerpts": [
    "FIRE investors aim to save a big chunk of their income while they're working so they can achieve financial freedom at a younger age and enjoy a long, fulfilling retirement.",
    "The 4% rule aims to help retirees find a safe withdrawal rate for each year in retirement. According to this rule, you can withdraw 4% of your total retirement savings in the first year and then adjust that amount for inflation in each subsequent year.",
    "Updates to the 4% rule for FIRE investors\nThe 4% rule may be right for investors with a 30-year retirement horizon. But others, including FIRE investors whose retirement horizon could be 50 years or more, will have better odds of making their savings last by customizing the 4% rule using Vanguard's principles of investing success.",
    "Traditional savers might save around 10%–15% of their income, whereas FIRE investors often save 50% or more."
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "财富自由（Financial Independence）指个人或家庭积累足够财务资源，无需依赖主动工作即可维持当前生活水平。FIRE（Financial Independence, Retire Early）运动倡导通过节俭生活、高比例储蓄和投资，在职业生涯早期实现财富自由。其核心原则包括4%安全提取率：从投资组合中第一年提取4%，之后按通胀调整，若此比例可覆盖年支出即视为财富自由。财富自由是主观概念，不同个体有不同的实现路径和生活标准。",
  "key_excerpts": [
    "Financial independence is a state where an individual or household has accumulated sufficient financial resources to cover its cost-of-living expenses without having to depend on active employment or work to earn money in order to maintain its current lifestyle.",
    "Some people practice frugal living, save and invest a large percentage of income to achieve financial independence early in their career, as evidenced by people following the \" financial independence retire early (FIRE)\" movement",
    "William Bengen conducted research to determine safe withdrawal rates from the portfolio and concluded that an individual can safely withdraw 4% of their portfolio savings in the first year of retirement and can adjust the withdrawal rate by rate of inflation in subsequent years.",
    "If an individual can cover their annual expenses by withdrawing 4% of their portfolio savings, the individual is assumed to have achieved financial independence.",
    "Financial independence is a subjective concept and can be interpreted differently by different individuals."
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "财务独立所需金额常用4%法则计算：退休第一年可提取储蓄的4%，之后每年按通胀调整，假设30年退休期。但FIRE投资者退休期可能长达50年，需调整：使用前瞻性回报预测、合理设定退休期限、降低费用、全球分散投资、采用动态支出策略。实际所需金额取决于个人开支、退休期限、收入来源等因素。",
  "key_excerpts": [
    "The 4% rule aims to help retirees find a safe withdrawal rate for each year in retirement. According to this rule, you can withdraw 4% of your total retirement savings in the first year and then adjust that amount for inflation in each subsequent year.",
    "Updates to the 4% rule for FIRE investors: Estimate future returns using forward-looking predictions; Set an appropriate retirement horizon; Minimize costs; Invest in a diversified portfolio; Use a dynamic spending strategy.",
    "The amount you need to save for retirement can vary significantly depending on your personal situation, your retirement horizon, and how much you anticipate spending in retirement."
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "财务独立所需金额的计算主要采用4%法则，即年开销乘以25得出目标资产。例如，年开销60万元则需1500万元。实际案例中，一位38岁软件工程师通过高储蓄率（50%）和投资ETF，8年后资产达目标70%，预计45岁实现财务自由。该法则基于历史数据，需考虑通胀、市场波动等因素调整。",
  "key_excerpts": [
    "計算方式：將您一年的總開銷乘以25，即為您所需的FIRE目標資產。公式為：FIRE目標資產 = 年開銷 x 25。",
    "範例：如果您每年生活開銷為新台幣60萬元，那麼您所需的FIRE目標資產就是 60萬 x 25 = 1,500萬元。",
    "【實務案例】：一位38歲的軟體工程師，月薪10萬元，透過嚴格的開銷管理，將儲蓄率提升至50%。他將每月5萬元投入高股息ETF與美股大盤ETF，並利用下班時間開發手機App增加額外收入。在持續8年後，他的資產已達到FIRE目標的70%，預計45歲即可實現財務自由。"
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "FIRE运动的核心原则是大幅降低开支、最大化储蓄、积极投资，以积累足够财富使工作成为可选项。财务独立（财富自由）指工作不再是生存必需，而是个人选择。运动倡导储蓄率通常达到50%-70%，并衍生出Fat FIRE、Lean FIRE、Barista FIRE和Coast FIRE等不同路径。其最大贡献在于将目标从单纯致富转向实现财务独立，即工作成为选择而非必需。",
  "key_excerpts": [
    "The FIRE movement is built around a simple idea: dramatically reduce your spending, maximize your savings, invest aggressively, and accumulate enough wealth to make work optional decades before the traditional retirement age.",
    "FIRE proponents frequently target savings rates between 50% and 70%, requiring a lifestyle built around extreme intentionality and delayed gratification.",
    "Perhaps the movement’s greatest contribution was shifting the goal from simply becoming wealthy to achieving financial independence—the point where work becomes a choice rather than a necessity.",
    "Fat FIRE – Retiring early while maintaining a comfortable or luxurious lifestyle, requiring substantial assets and typically a high income.\nLean FIRE – The original minimalist approach, emphasizing extremely low living expenses to reach financial independence as quickly as possible.\nBarista FIRE – Leaving a demanding full-time career while working part-time to cover living expenses and often secure health insurance.\nCoast FIRE – Saving aggressively early in life until investments are projected to grow on their own, allowing future earnings to cover only current living expenses.",
    "Financial independence isn’t simply about escaping work. It’s about creating choices."
  ]
}

